{"id": "EUVD-2026-86025", "enisaUuid": "250afacd-9aa2-373d-abc1-1f96050328c4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npds_core: quiesce DMA before freeing resources\n\npdsc_teardown() frees DMA buffers but does not disable bus mastering,\nleaving the device able to perform DMA after the buffers are freed.\nThis can lead to use-after-free if the device writes to freed memory.\n\nAdd pci_clear_master() to pdsc_teardown() to disable bus mastering\nbefore freeing resources, ensuring all DMA is quiesced.\n\nAdd pci_set_master() to pdsc_setup() to re-enable bus mastering,\nwhich is needed for the firmware recovery path since pdsc_teardown()\nnow disables it.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84fc3f30b87e06a11d1807cd385603522610ed40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc8beb70e70fc90e54efdbc1128cf7de799e6be4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9eee6b90bee3df496ed9094d9e76d5e478d72d0a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6443f4f20bdae726fe01cf5946fba9742a0ffda6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97412", "GHSA-vh7w-pf8m-646h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02a3262d-fd53-3210-b614-d21156d969f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2a538386-fa5a-3936-b268-31825d8f2e59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "2dc9c4ce-009b-3b38-87c5-01b62cba883a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "463fdd3f-b179-3e2a-b7ff-50a9223cbab8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "45d76f492938cdc27ddadc16e1e75103f4cfbf56 <6443f4f20bdae726fe01cf5946fba9742a0ffda6"}, {"id": "5e9e68c3-63c6-33be-b107-4d961e16e216", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "61026697-c10f-38e3-80ee-b7c85ff3c29d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "45d76f492938cdc27ddadc16e1e75103f4cfbf56 <cc8beb70e70fc90e54efdbc1128cf7de799e6be4"}, {"id": "909b5a78-dbb6-3f0d-b440-f0f7d73f51f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "9c54cc9d-f8cd-320f-bd28-6251a48017ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "45d76f492938cdc27ddadc16e1e75103f4cfbf56 <84fc3f30b87e06a11d1807cd385603522610ed40"}, {"id": "d8cf8ee9-78de-3ded-9f3a-b432926e82cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "45d76f492938cdc27ddadc16e1e75103f4cfbf56 <9eee6b90bee3df496ed9094d9e76d5e478d72d0a"}, {"id": "e81c0095-5f2e-3507-b883-4a5d0f0a295f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f8e52045-621c-3b16-ae77-d09a06063e05", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}